                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Donna, a one-woman business owner in Lake County, shared how she \"relies on ACA subsidies to help pay for insurance to mitigate soaring healthcare costs in mountain communities.\"\n\nWithout these subsidies, to keep her current plan, which has a $7,000 deductible, it will cost an additional $10,000 in 2026. As Donna said, \"these costs are not sustainable,\" and the sudden loss of subsidies could force her and \"many hardworking Americans to forego insurance by the New Year.\" We cannot let that happen\u2014 it means costs will go up for EVERYONE.",
